  </section>

  <section class="founder" id="founder">
    <div class="wrap">
      <figure class="sheet">
        <img src="/images/founder.jpg" alt="Tito Kishan Vemuri" width="640" height="640" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption class="cap"><b>Fig. 3</b> Tito Kishan Vemuri</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>The founder</h2>
        <p>Tito Kishan Vemuri spent two decades, 1995 to 2014, in senior engineering and technology roles at GE Energy, GE Aviation and Tata Consulting Engineers, leading technical innovation, operational excellence and IP generation. He started Proinn in 2015.</p>
        <p>As IP leader for GE Energy's India engineering operation he ran innovation workouts for 750+ engineers. The result was 850+ US patents filed in about six years, one gold patent holder with 25 patents and about 20 silver holders with 10 each.</p>
        <p>He holds one granted US patent from GE, three filed Indian patents and 10 registered trademarks, among them Invent in India®.</p>
        <h3>Standing</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>India's first TRIZ level 4 specialist, 2024. MATRIZ-certified level 3 practitioner since 2011.</li>
          <li>Elected MATRIZ board member, 2024–26. Appointed Vice President for TRIZ deployment in India, November 2022. TRIZ Champion 2022.</li>
          <li>One of about 20 MATRIZ-accredited CEM representatives worldwide, licence 063/02-2024/1. The only Indian with this accreditation.</li>
          <li>Founder chairman of TRIZTI®, India's regional MATRIZ association. Organised seven editions of Bharat TRIZutsav®, 2016 to 2022, sponsored by Tata Sons, GE, TVS Motor and MATRIZ.</li>
          <li>Member, CII national committee for R&amp;D, innovation and technology since 2018. Assessor, CII industrial innovation awards 2019 to 2021. Management committee, SAE Bengaluru.</li>
          <li>Master Black Belt, GE USA 2012. DFSS Black Belt, GE USA 2006. IP analyst, GE and Fletcher Yoder 2009.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Record</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>100+ MATRIZ certification workshops at levels 1, 2 and 3 since 2015, and 1000+ inventors groomed. Clients report product cost savings in millions of dollars and many disclosures filed as patents.</li>
          <li>Taught in nine countries: India, Chile, UAE, Malaysia, Thailand, Singapore, Indonesia, Vietnam and the Philippines. The only Indian to give TRIZ keynotes across Asia.</li>
          <li>As operational excellence coach to AirAsia, delivered year-on-year savings of millions of dollars.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>He learnt TRIZ under Dr Sergei Ikovenko, TRIZ Master, president of DFP-Institute and chairman of MATRIZ CEM, who co-teaches the level 2 and 3 workshops.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

